    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.81) anchoring the lineup as our most potent offensive threats. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to a soft matchup against the 4.84 xERA of Lowder, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start despite the platoon disadvantage against Wilkinson; his pedigree and the favorable matchup (4.63 xERA) keep his floor safely in the high-60s. We are also high on **Henry Bolte** (65.23), who receives a significant 10% park boost today; when paired with an aggressive lead-off spot, he presents a high-upside play that heavily leverages our focus on sprint speed and base-stealing potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Dominic Smith** (43.84) ultimately fell short of the starting rotation. While **Dominic Smith** offers a decent platoon edge against the right-handed Ralston, he was pushed out by the higher efficiency scores of **Andy Pages** and **Tommy White**, both of whom benefit from superior ballpark environmental factors. Managers should keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Liam Hicks**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tommy White**. While we have modeled these based on historical positioning, any significant drop in batting order\u2014specifically for **Sam Antonacci** or **Henry Bolte**\u2014could result in a downward revision of their daily efficiency scores. Currently, we are monitoring all lineups closely to ensure the Austin Waves remain positioned to capitalize on every available stolen base opportunity.",
